Before US Victim's Torture, His Neighbor Had a Similar Experience
Dr. Richard Pearson tells the story of his neighbor. He believes that it illustrates that US technology with inserted voice and cognitive violence is out of control - and denigrating the entire constitutional order.
The Neighbor
Dr. Richard Pearson wants to be very careful in describing a neighbor's experience in 2024–2025. Unlike the true stories that he tells about himself, he wants to avoid many details. This is not his story. Nevertheless, it is real.
"I have a neighbor - an African American woman. In the second half of 2024, she began experiencing symptoms. They came suddenly. Nothing had changed in her life. Family, friends, daily routine. Then, something began to happen almost overnight. Whenever she was watching television, she would get these thoughts of "death" and "dying". As the months progressed, she couldn't watch television much at all because the triggers were numerous. She turned to music. That helped somewhat. Then, the thoughts would persist even when she wasn't watching television.
Her friends and I would get on the phone with her and counsel her through the ordeal that stretched into 2025. Her crying and distress really pained us - seeing her go through this. We recommended diet and lifestyle changes. We listened. We comforted her. I never once thought that it was psychological - as in a mental break. I really didn't. I have known this lady for years. She is a dear friend of mind - a brilliant mind.
I remember, though, a very specific detail in her story. The thoughts of "death" and "dying" that were inundating her were not accompanied by any thoughts about suicide. She said this repeatedly, even remarked how strange it sounded. I believed her. I logged that in my mind because clinically, it is unusual. "Death" and "dying" without suicide causes one's ears to perk up. Perhaps, a terminal diagnosis of an illness could theoretically explain the discontinuity. She didn't have that. Her health was fine. Eventually, she found some medical solutions to help with it."
The Resistance
"Now, more than a year after the torture campaign against me began, I am looking at this case with my friend and neighbor entirely different. I know that there are numerous technological forms of inserted voice violence. This form of violence has become deeply normalized - endemic - in the US. I also know that it is designed to mimic mental illness, which is why cases have seemed to remain on the margins of society.
There is an important similarity between my neighbor and me. We are both strong community advocates - though different in scope. We resist structural and interpersonal racism. We devise strategies to prevent harm and to encourage justice and community.
I think that she was targeted. I really do. The unusual facts of her case - started with her watching television, intense thoughts of death without suicide, and a sudden onset - strongly suggest to me something highly unusual. It doesn't involve her health or mind as the source.
There is an important fact. Her living room faces the street. It could have been a portable device in a parked vehicle - using some sort of radar to detect when she was in her home in front of her television, then utilizing the technology - rather, engaging in violence. It could have been in the air, as I have discovered on many occasions. It sounds like science fiction, but we need to accept that this technology exists. What is in museums with ultrasonic voice insertion has been scaled, weaponized, and taken different forms. I almost certainly know more than the average member of Congress about the proliferation and capability of this technology.
